{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he uncovered himself inside his tent.</b> It is written אהלה (with the possessive suffix), inside his wife's tent — this teaches that the pleasure of much wine leads to much conjugal relations." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> 'Inside his tent (אהלה)' alludes to Samaria, which is called אהלה (Hosea 5:13); for they were exiled only on account of wine, as it is said (Isaiah 28:7) ״וגם אלה ביין שגו ובשכר תעו״, and on this account Scripture used the expression ויתגל ('and he uncovered himself')."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:26.857244909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}